<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30747" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐθάς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>, ὁ, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>accustomed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. γενέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					1.12
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. γενέσθαι τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.44
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εῖναι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Oth.</u>
				5
			</span></i>; of persons, <i>familiar</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				8.30
			</span></i>: c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ νούσῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Morb.Sacr.</u>
					12
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				5.499
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of things,
				<i>customary, usual</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοῦσοι ἐ. ἀπὸ νεότητος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					2.125
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡδονή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.316
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>tame</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				22.273c
			</span></i>.</div>
